WEBVTT

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:11.300
To fight against messengers from the future who are changing history to erase soccer...

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.930
...we, the Raimon Eleven, are now traveling through time to assemble the strongest eleven in history.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.100
Hey, hey!

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.620
What does it say?

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:33.320
These criminals called the White Deer Gang kidnapped children, but now those children have been rescued.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.570
And it wasn't done by the police or the samurai.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.330
They say it was a young man.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.390
Wow! What's his name?

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:45.330
His surname is Kinoshita and his name is Toukichirou.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.880
Kinoshita Toukichirou?

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.390
That's so amazing!

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:56.180
While it was really us who took back the children by beating the White Deer Gang in a soccer battle,

00:00:56.180 --> 00:01:01.050
historically it's Toukichirou-san who lives in this era that was made to have done it.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.160
I see.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.980
So what we do in the past gets reflected in this way.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:08.080
Yeah.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:57.240
We're back!

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.810
Oh, welcome back.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.300
Huh? Where's Shindou-senpai?

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.080
Shindou?

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:08.060
I sent Shindou out to train so he can Mixi-max with Nobunaga.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:13.580
The banquet for cherry blossom viewing held by Nobunaga will be our chance to Mixi-max.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:19.610
Until then, he needs to make himself a bigger vessel in order to take in Nobunaga's aura.

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.370
I see.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:25.160
Let's prepare for the Great Dancer Strategy in the meantime.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:25.620
Yeah.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.870
Then let me reiterate the plan.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:36.470
First, we will infiltrate the banquet as dancers.

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:40.310
While Nobunaga's attention is focused on our dancing,

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:45.990
I will use the Mixi-max gun on him for the five seconds it takes to receive Nobunaga's aura.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:51.130
Our problem is what dance we should use to distract Nobunaga.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.320
Let's use a dance from our time.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.480
Since it's from the future, he'll like it because it's something new.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:00.690
If you want something new, the dance from my time won't be beat.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.250
Is that a challenge I hear?

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.110
Bring it on!

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:10.930
Neither of them have any rhythm...

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.970
They're both rejected.

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:14.770
Anyone here who's danced before?

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:19.700
Right. It won't go that conveniently.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:22.670
I think we should choose a dance that's closer to this era than from the future.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:29.460
If a really wild dance ends up getting popular here, it will change the timeline.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:30.840
I see.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.810
But what dances are in this era?

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:35.360
How about the Bon dance?

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:38.330
Yeah, maybe the Bon dance will work.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:43.560
I don't know how old it is but it's been around for ages and it's rather Japanese-ish.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:44.560
Yeah!

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:45.960
Aoi, can you dance it?

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:51.780
I've danced it a few times, but I don't remember every detail.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:54.320
Teach us! You can just give us what you know.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:57.430
We'll all put our heads together for the parts you don't remember.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:00.270
Okay then...

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:09.680
And a one, two, three, four!

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.550
One, two, three, four!

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:15.990
One, two, three!

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:18.000
One, two! One, two!

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:18.810
One, two, three!

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:20.940
One, two, three, four!

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:20.960
Is this all right?

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:23.090
No, no!

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:26.030
Rhythm, the steps, and heart, they're all unacceptable!

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:30.150
At this rate, your job to keep Nobunaga mesmerized will be a dream within a dream!

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:31.840
I don't want to hear that from you.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:34.550
But Wondeba does have a point.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:39.850
At this level, we may end up getting chased out of the banquet hall.

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:41.470
What should we do...

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:44.420
Do you want to get better at dancing?

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.150
Tasuke!

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:48.590
Want me to ask my sis to help you?

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:49.970
Okatsu-san?

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:54.730
She has to help out at the store, so she can't stay for very long though.

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:56.140
That's okay!

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:57.140
Can you ask her?

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:58.460
Sure!

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:02.850
Besides, I want to help you out as thanks for saving us from the White Deer Gang yesterday.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:04.760
Thank you, Tasuke!

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:07.390
But I want to ask a favor in exchange.

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:07.990
What is it?

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:12.720
That game you call soccer... I want to play it with you again.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:16.180
Sure! Let's play soccer!

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:22.920
I'm not that good at dancing, but if that's okay with you...

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:25.670
Please help us!

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.890
And, here we go!

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:43.610
To the right.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:44.840
To the left.

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:46.240
And one, two, three.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:48.960
Yes, they're in synchronization!

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:51.780
At this rate it's possible, it's just poss-

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.380
You again.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.080
We still have a far ways to go.

00:06:56.630 --> 00:06:58.330
In that case...!

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:01.790
Huh? Tsurugi isn't here.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:03.960
He left for somewhere a few minutes ago.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:05.930
Ran away, did he.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:08.390
Takuto-sama isn't here either.

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.880
They said he's practicing soccer at the other side.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:12.800
I see.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:15.750
Shin-sama, I'll go to cheer for you right now!

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:18.260
You haven't remembered all the steps yet!

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:20.080
Shin-sama!

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:24.060
Will we really be able to capture Nobunaga's attention with this?

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:26.650
Yay!

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:34.170
Since I can't rely on their dancing, my skills with the gun will become very important.

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:39.670
After all, I will need to keep the beam of light on Nobunaga for five seconds.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:41.480
Let's do this!

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:55.650
Mixi-max...

00:07:55.650 --> 00:08:00.350
<i>Make yourself a bigger vessel so that you may take in Nobunaga's aura.</i>

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.690
How do I take in his aura?

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:06.830
How do I make myself a bigger vessel?

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:08.810
Am I even able to do it?

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:15.000
<i>Instrumentalist Maestro!</i>

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:17.260
<i>Armed!</i>

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:26.240
I haven't even learned how to use Avatar Armed.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:32.470
But I need to win if I want to protect soccer and change our timeline back to normal.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:33.930
Takuto-sama.

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:36.750
Okatsu-san.

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:40.320
Are you feeling ill somewhere?

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:42.780
No, it's not like that.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:46.460
There are times when that happens.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.190
Um...

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:56.630
Eating pure white tofu will make your heart pure white as well, and you'll feel better again.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:00.630
Thank you.

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:02.640
Go on, have some.

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:13.320
When I look at you, I think that it must be hard work making tofu from early morning to late at night.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:16.590
That's not so. It's pretty fun.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:21.870
But the water seems cold, and handling all of that load seems like grueling work...

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:22.790
Even then?

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:23.950
Yes.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:27.600
Just as you say, the work is hard.

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:33.150
But when I'm able to make that pure white tofu, I get such a great feeling.

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:34.690
Great feeling...

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:40.140
Everyone who eats this tofu says that it's delicious.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:46.110
When I see their smiles, whatever had given me so much trouble making it just washes away.

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:49.220
They make me feel a warmth that spreads throughout my heart.

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:51.440
That's wonderful.

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:52.710
Yes.

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:55.710
It's the same for you, isn't it?

00:09:55.710 --> 00:10:00.230
You love soccer just as much as I love tofu, don't you?

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.690
Love soccer...

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:07.100
Oh... I'd forgotten how that felt.

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:09.050
I see!

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:10.400
Perhaps...

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:13.080
Thank you, Okatsu-san.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:15.510
See? Don't you feel better now?

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:16.730
Yeah.

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:20.270
I must go back to the store.

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:22.920
Do your best, Takuto-sama.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:30.040
Tenma said it one time...

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:35.990
That maybe Avatars are our love for soccer that have taken form.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:41.750
If joining my feelings to my Avatar is what will make me complete Avatar Armed...

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:46.040
...I shouldn't forget what it feels like to love soccer.

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:55.480
Instrumentalist Maestro!

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:58.200
Armed!

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.470
There's no mistake.

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:05.150
This is that feeling!

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:18.760
I don't know if completing Avatar Armed will bring me closer to completing Mixi-max.

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:21.990
But for now, I'll just have to believe!

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:23.660
I see you've caught on to something.

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:25.440
Fei.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.800
Let me help you.

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:28.610
Thanks.

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:30.690
Fei.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:31.310
What's up?

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:36.990
The reason you want to protect soccer is because you love it too, right?

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:39.100
No, that's not it.

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:44.030
The word "love" isn't enough to express my feelings.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:47.760
That's because soccer is everything to me.

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:49.900
Everything...

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:51.680
I see, it's that important to you...

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:54.280
Come on, one more time!

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:55.580
Yeah!

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:58.380
Changes in history...

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:03.880
They tell me that there was a change where my injured brother was able to continue playing soccer.

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:10.600
If that's true, then I have to do my best for both myself and my brother who gave soccer back to me.

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:13.410
To protect soccer...

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:16.460
<i>Soccer is everything to me.</i>

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:20.380
Soccer is everything?

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:24.390
All right!

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:26.630
The dance is perfect!

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:28.040
What are you talking about?

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:30.370
Tenma.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:34.590
I thought soccer was a little silly at first.

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:42.600
But after trying it out, I learned a lot.

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:47.490
Like how kicking isn't the only thing, or how you need to predict where the ball goes next.

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:49.980
Or how to compete for the ball by not being afraid to fight for it.

00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:52.850
A lot of things, really.

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:57.370
It was so much fun learning all of that.

00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:00.370
That's why I want to learn more.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:04.210
About soccer, about you guys, about so many things!

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:05.370
Yeah!

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:06.320
Let's go!

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:12.820
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:18.240
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:24.470
The banquet for cherry blossom viewing is finally today!

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:29.480
Shindou, our plan depends on whether or not you are able to take in Nobunaga's aura.

00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:30.320
Are you ready?

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:32.180
I don't know.

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.080
I'm sure you can do it.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:37.190
I'm sure Shindou-kun will be able to Mixi-max.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:39.890
I believe in you.

00:13:39.890 --> 00:13:41.030
Fei...

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.680
Okay then, we're counting on you, Shindou!

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:46.090
All right!

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:49.120
Let's dance till we drop!

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:51.550
Nishiki, these are for you.

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:54.240
You're in charge of the taiko drum.

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:57.750
Why?!!!

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:01.340
Shindou, Tsurugi, you two take the flutes.

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:03.510
Even if you gave that to me, I don't know how to play.

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:04.970
That won't be a problem.

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:07.270
I prepared this!

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:12.980
If I don't actually have to play drums, then let me dance!

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:15.680
Now, let us be off! The banquet awaits!

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:27.960
I should be able to see the dances from up here.

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:30.530
Now, where are Tenma and the others?

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:34.290
It looks like there's an interview to decide who goes inside.

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:38.320
You girls are beautiful, so you pass.

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:41.350
The problem is that interviewer there.

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:44.490
You guys are too good-looking, so you fail.

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:45.630
He's so fickle.

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:47.330
Will we be okay?

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:49.280
Of course we'll be okay.

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:55.370
Now this is something...

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:59.070
Very good, very good!

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:03.100
This is...

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:05.380
This one is tricky...

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:08.840
We pass.

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:10.680
Fail!

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:17.500
I can't have Nobunaga-sama feel ill upon seeing this!

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:19.200
Leave, leave!

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:21.930
This is your fault, Nishiki!

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:23.850
I thought it was totally funny!

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:26.880
That man doesn't know good comedy when he sees it!

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:28.990
What do we do, Tenma?

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:32.560
We need to get in somehow if we want to take Nobunaga's aura.

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:37.920
Okay, you pass.

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:42.680
Hey, you there!

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:45.250
You can't mix with a different group!

00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:48.360
Okay, you pass.

00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:50.660
Wait!

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:54.710
Get out!

00:15:55.990 --> 00:16:00.060
We've come to assist since we heard you don't have any waitresses.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.890
You can't disguise yourselves either!

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:08.170
Come on, Tenma, don't tell me you can't get inside.

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:13.200
What do we do now?

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:17.150
We won't get a chance to dance after we practiced so hard!

00:16:17.150 --> 00:16:19.310
That's not our main issue here.

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:22.390
Daisuke-san, do you know of a good way?

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:25.400
He's sleeping...

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:28.800
So laid-back, is he?

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:31.320
I'll smash him to pieces with these drumsticks!

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:33.700
This is all your fault to begin with!

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:36.950
We will no longer be accepting any more dancers!

00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:40.760
What are you doing, Tenma?!

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:42.680
What do we do, what do we do?!

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:44.440
We'll just have to bulldoze our way inside!

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:46.770
Don't go trying to make things even worse!

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:52.770
We need Nobunaga's aura to form the strongest eleven in history...

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:49.040
Then what else do we do?!

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:51.720
Don't look at me!

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:54.610
Hey, if it isn't Tenma!

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:56.780
Toukichirou-san!

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:59.780
What are you doing here?

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:05.950
I didn't want to miss this chance of getting a glimpse at Nobunaga-sama, even from afar.

00:17:05.950 --> 00:17:08.520
Toukichirou-san, were you given an invitation?

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:11.660
No, but it's easy to get in...

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:12.980
...by using this.

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:15.740
But we can't get in anymore.

00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:17.800
So, use this.

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:24.720
Toukichirou-san, can you help me with something?

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:29.210
What?! So you're those legendary people?!

00:17:29.850 --> 00:17:35.220
Tenma of the Matsukaze family is so famous for dancing that even the Imperial Court asks for you!

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:36.190
What?!

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:41.310
I can't believe skilled dancers such as yourselves would be turned away...

00:17:41.310 --> 00:17:44.850
Dear me, I would find that unthinkable!

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:50.120
What would Nobunaga-sama have to say when he finds out that he missed seeing your dancing?

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:54.280
Oh! I'm so sorry for holding you back.

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:55.940
Please, go on your way.

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:56.830
W-Wait!

00:17:57.430 --> 00:18:05.300
I-I have made special arrangements to give you special permission to attend the banquet.

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:10.850
Looks like they managed to slip inside.

00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:21.530
There's Nobunaga!

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:28.290
Yes, thank you.

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:33.760
Next, we will show you the dancers of Tenma from the Matsukaze family.

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:35.330
I leave the rest to you.

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:38.490
It's their turn! Good luck!

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:43.550
Please look forward to a wonderful performance from the legendary dancers who are said to have danced in the Imperial Court!

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:49.610
Good luck, Takuto-sama.

00:19:03.810 --> 00:19:05.760
It's them...

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:06.600
But...

00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:13.740
What are they doing?!

00:19:13.740 --> 00:19:16.150
They're so nervous that they're all disorganized!

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:19.610
They'll never hold Nobunaga's attention at this rate...

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:23.860
What are you going to do? That Nobunaga is looking annoyed!

00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:25.320
Tenma...

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:27.730
What do we do?!

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:30.050
Nobunaga isn't liking our dance at all.

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:33.790
At this rate, we'll never get his aura.

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:35.980
What should we do?

00:19:39.850 --> 00:19:41.250
Toukichirou-san?

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:45.340
Tenma, show him your real charm!

00:19:46.070 --> 00:19:46.850
I get it!

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:49.400
We have this!

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:01.900
T-Tenma!

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:03.380
It isn't dancing we should be doing.

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:06.600
It's soccer!

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:07.660
I see!

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:09.090
Shindou-senpai!

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:14.830
If we show off our soccer, rather than a dance filled with pretense...

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:17.670
It has a greater chance of pulling in people's attention!

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:21.970
Oh, I don't know what's going on here anymore!

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:39.880
Let's go!

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:49.290
No way!

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:52.210
Wondeba!

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:54.540
Villains!

00:20:57.810 --> 00:20:59.570
Isn't that one....

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:01.440
...with the rest of them?

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:05.980
These insolent knaves were plotting to kill you, Nobunaga-sama!

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:08.470
Look! Here is the proof!

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:56.840
A kemari battle to decide who rules the country begins!

00:22:56.840 --> 00:23:00.870
C'mon, guys! Let's make new hissatsu techniques to win!

00:23:00.870 --> 00:23:03.690
Next, Training in the Owari Province!

00:23:03.690 --> 00:23:05.310
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:19.620
The Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone's proverb today is...

00:23:21.760 --> 00:23:27.090
Eating pure white tofu will make your heart pure white as well, and you'll feel better again.

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:27.850
That's all!
